1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,276
Most real robots come as URDF files.

2
00:00:03,276 --> 00:00:08,518
In this module you import Carter, a two wheeled robot with a caster,

3
00:00:08,518 --> 00:00:13,222
using the rewritten URDF importer in Isaac Sim six point one.

4
00:00:14,122 --> 00:00:15,577
Here is the pipeline.

5
00:00:15,577 --> 00:00:20,429
The importer converts the URDF into a USD file plus a payloads folder.

6
00:00:20,429 --> 00:00:26,251
New in six point one, the physics lives in a variant set with one option per engine.

7
00:00:26,251 --> 00:00:30,965
Until you select the physx variant, the robot has no physics at all.

8
00:00:30,965 --> 00:00:36,718
And the importer no longer configures drives, so you set the wheel drives yourself.

9
00:00:37,618 --> 00:00:38,565
Let's import.

10
00:00:38,565 --> 00:00:41,188
You do not need the course download.

11
00:00:41,188 --> 00:00:46,872
The same Carter URDF ships with Isaac Sim, and a copy is in the assets folder.

12
00:00:46,872 --> 00:00:50,370
Use File, Import, and select carter dot u r d f.

13
00:00:50,370 --> 00:00:56,200
In the options panel, set the base type to mobile, because Carter drives around.

14
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:57,147
Click import.

15
00:00:57,147 --> 00:01:00,135
The converted robot opens as a new stage.

16
00:01:01,035 --> 00:01:02,892
Expand it in the stage panel.

17
00:01:02,892 --> 00:01:07,374
Links live under Geometry, with chassis link as the articulation root.

18
00:01:07,374 --> 00:01:12,688
Joints live under Physics: the two driven wheels and the two passive caster joints.

19
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:16,082
And on the top prim there is the physics variant set.

20
00:01:16,982 --> 00:01:18,869
Two steps make it usable.

21
00:01:18,869 --> 00:01:24,076
Select carter, open variants in the property panel, and choose physx.

22
00:01:24,076 --> 00:01:30,416
Give the two wheel joints a velocity drive: stiffness zero and damping ten thousand.

23
00:01:30,416 --> 00:01:35,699
Leave the caster joints passive, with zero stiffness and zero damping.

24
00:01:35,699 --> 00:01:36,077
Save.

25
00:01:36,077 --> 00:01:38,794
Your Carter is now a drivable robot.

